      "name": "Burhinus",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "Thick-knees — nocturnal waders named for their prominent, swollen-looking knee joints (actually the ankle). Their large yellow eyes have excellent night vision, allowing them to hunt insects and small vertebrates under cover of darkness. By day they rely on their cryptic plumage to remain invisible against stones and dry earth. Their haunting, wailing calls at dusk are characteristic of open stony landscapes.",
